      "created_at": "2019-01-28T14:27:58Z",
      "updated_at": "2019-01-28T14:27:58Z",
      "body": ">I assume it is a breach of privacy to show if someone has/hasn't claimed an ID, plus we may not want anyone to see how responsive/unresponsive various delegates are.\r\n\r\nThis information is present in the public developer dump, so even if we remove the view on this the information would still be public.\r\nIf we want to hide this information, we should probably set the `delegate_id_to_handle_wca_id_claim` to nil when dumping the database.\r\n\r\nIt should also been noted that a pending claim hanging there may not always be a sign of unresponsiveness: the Delegate may simply be waiting on a copy of a form of identification from the claimer.\r\n\r\nI don't have a strong opinion on whether or not this information should be private; but if it should we should handle this in the database dumper.",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
      "reactions": {
